---
#2832: a `system` case calls a service whose result is a refined type of a
commons the context under test `uses`. The harness is named for its target, so
its `uses` entry used to replace the target's, the target's consumed view lost
the commons type, and the call typed as `()` (`bynk.effect.bind_on_non_effect`).
---
suite boundary.consumer as system {
  case "price crosses back" {
    let r <- boundary.consumer.askPrice(1)
    expect r is Err(_)
  }
}
